===Etymology 2===
{{dercat|nl|odt|gmw-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|nl|dum|wedde}}, from a byform of {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*wadą}}, whence {{m|nl|wad}}. Closely related with {{cog|gmh|wete}}, {{m|gmh|wettin|g=f|t=drinking place, shallow pond}}. The Dutch appears to require a neuter {{m|gem-pro||*wadją}} (though feminine use is also attested), the High German a feminine īn-stem {{m|gem-pro||*wadį̄}}.

